0	section	Investigating the skeleton
1	box	The skeleton seems fresh. It looks like the bones have been gnawed clean fairly recently.
1	line	Player	There's also a scrawled note. It's barely readable...
1	line	Player	Well, that's not exactly reassuring.
1	line	Player	Uhh... Nice piggy?
1	cond	If the player is not wearing Gnome goggles:
2	line	Player	Argh! My eyes!
1	cond	If the player is wearing Gnome goggles:
2	line	Player	Argh! My eyes! The goggles do nothing!
1	box	Some time passes...
1	line	Pig Thing	*Sniff* *Sniff*
1	line	Pig Thing	*Snort*
1	line	Player	...
1	line	Spria	Well then, what do we have here?
1	line	Spria	Still breathing, eh...?
1	line	Spria	Seems I came at just the right time.
1	line	Spria	We'd better get you out of here before that thing returns.
1	line	Player	W-what happened? Where am I?
1	action	end
0	section	Attempting to enter the Sourhog cave after being attacked by the Sourhog
1	line	Player	I think I find out more about that monster from Spria in Draynor Village before heading back down there.
1	action	end
0	section	The Sourhog
0	section	Talking to Spria
0	section	Initial conversation
1	line	Spria	Oh, you're awake!
1	line	Player	Who are you? How did I end up here?
1	line	Spria	My name's Spria and I'm a slayer master. You've had a nasty encounter with a Sourhog.
1	line	Player	A Sourhog? You mean the giant pig monster?
1	line	Spria	Precisely. You're extremely lucky that I found you. Another few hours and you'd have been hog chow.
1	line	Spria	Were you responding to Sarah's bounty too?
1	line	Player	Yes... It sounded like an easy few coins...
1	line	Spria	I thought as much. I found you on the floor of the cave, you must have been knocked unconscious.
1	line	Player	That thing caught me completely off-guard. Normally I can handle myself in a fight, but its spitting attack is pretty fearsome!
1	cond	If the player's inventory is full:
2	line	Spria	I have an item for you that will help you on your quest, but you don't seem to have enough space. Come and see me again when you've cleared some room.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player's inventory is not full:
2	line	Spria	The beast's saliva is extremely acidic and your eyes are most vulnerable. It'll cause terrible injuries and leave you unable to attack or defend yourself very well.
2	line	Player	So how am I supposed to handle that?
2	line	Spria	Luckily, the Slayer skill provides us with an array of useful equipment and techniques for dealing with... special foes.
2	line	Spria	In the case of our Sourhog, you'll be needing these.
2	box	Spria hands you a pair of Reinforced Goggles.
2	action	
2	line	Spria	This eyewear will protect you from the spitting attack, allowing you to fight the monster on equal terms.
2	line	Spria	Most enemies have a weakness, too. The Sourhog's thick hide provides excellent protection against slashing and insulates it from magic damage.
2	line	Spria	You'd be best trying to pierce it with arrows or a stabbing weapon.
2	line	Spria	Go now, the bounty is all yours to claim. I suggest you recoup your strength and head back to fight it using your new goggles.
2	line	Spria	If you make it out alive, collect your bounty and then come see me so that we can speak further.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Why are you helping me?
3	line	Player	Why are you helping me?
3	line	Spria	Well, I suppose I could have left you in there to be eaten...
3	line	Spria	But you know what that'd make me? A monster. And as a slayer master, that's really not a great look.
3	line	Spria	Besides, my father always taught me that knowledge is worth more than gold. I'm happy to sacrifice a few coins in order to pass my experience on to you.
3	line	Player	Well, I sure am glad you were there to lend a hand. Thank you!
3	line	Spria	Don't mention it. Was there something else?
3	action	other
2	option	How did I end up back in Draynor Village?
3	line	Player	How did I end up back in Draynor Village?
3	line	Spria	I carried you out and dragged you back here to my house to recover, it really wasn't easy. You're welcome to rest here for as long as you need.
3	line	Spria	Was there something else?
3	action	other
2	option	You said you were a slayer master. What's that?
3	line	Player	You said you were a slayer master. What's that?
3	line	Spria	There are many of us. We're experts in the ancient art of monster slaying. People from across Gielinor come to us for tasks and advice.
3	line	Spria	Well... actually, I'm fairly new to this. I've been learning from my father, Turael, for many years. We decided it was finally time for me to continue the family profession.
3	line	Spria	Was there something else?
3	action	other
2	option	Can I have another pair of Reinforced Goggles?
3	line	Player	Can I have another pair of Reinforced Goggles?
3	cond	If the player has a pair equipped:
4	line	Spria	No, you're still wearing the last pair I gave you!
4	line	Spria	Was there something else?
4	action	other
3	cond	If the player has a pair in their inventory:
4	line	Spria	You've still got the last one I gave you, it's there in your inventory! Those things aren't cheap, you know.
4	line	Spria	Was there something else?
4	action	other
3	cond	If the player has a pair in their bank:
4	line	Spria	I know many people all across Gielinor, and my sources tell me you still have the last one in your bank.
4	line	Spria	Was there something else?
4	action	other
3	cond	If a player does not have a pair in their inventory or bank:
4	line	Spria	Sure, I have another going spare. Please try to take better care of these.
4	action	"Spria hands you another pair of Reinforced Goggles."
4	line	Spria	Was there something else?
4	action	other
2	option	What can you tell me about the Sourhog?
3	line	Player	What can you tell me about the Sourhog?
3	line	Spria	Well, I'm not much of a history buff... But I'll tell you what I know.
3	line	Spria	Many years back, before even I was around, there were two rival family farms not far from where we're standing.
3	line	Spria	Every year the village would hold a 'Finest Swine in Show' prize at the annual faire.
3	line	Spria	The same farmer would win year after year without fail. Driven mad with jealousy, his rival decided to hire a dodgy dark wizard to give him an edge over the competition.
3	line	Spria	The wizard attempted to alter the pig's appearance. I'm sure you can guess how well that went!
3	line	Spria	Long story short, the mutant, what we now know as a Sourhog, went on a brief rampage and escaped.
3	line	Spria	It must have somehow managed to reproduce, because people have reported seeing them in groups.
3	line	Spria	Up until now, so long as they were left alone, they'd keep to themselves. Rumours are, they live in deep underground caverns, scavenging what they can find.
3	line	Spria	But if they're living so close-by and attacking people on roads, then... they must be getting bold and trying to resurface.
3	line	Spria	Was there something else?
3	action	other
2	option	That'll be all for now.
3	line	Player	That'll be all for now.
3	line	Spria	Very well. Good luck, slayer.
3	action	end
